  "metadata": {
    "title": "Harmonised boundary layer wind profile dataset from six ground-based doppler wind lidars in a transect across Paris (France) from 2022-06-10 to 2024-03-05",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17710093",
    "publication_date": "2025-11-25",
    "description": "<p>Quality controlled and harmonized dataset on wind direction and wind speed profiles from ground-based Doppler Wind LIDARS (DWL), deployed in a multi-institutional effort along a 40 km transect through the centre of the Paris Metropolitan area (France) for the period 2022-06-10 to 2024-03-05.</p>\n<p>The dataset, its derivation, quality control and evaluation against radiosondes and in-situ observations are decribed in the following manuscript:</p>\n<p>Morrison, W., Looschelders, D., C&eacute;spedes, J., Claxton, B., Drouin, M.-A., Dupont, J.-C., Faucheux, A., Haeffelin, M., Holst, C. C., Kotthaus, S., Masson, V., McGregor, J., Price, J., Zeeman, M., Grimmond, S., and Christen, A.: Harmonised boundary layer wind profile dataset from six ground-based doppler wind lidars in a transect across Paris, France, <em>Earth Syst. Sci. Data</em>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-2025-167\">https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-2025-167</a>, 2025.</p>\n<p>Preview graphs for the full dataset on a daily basis (wind speed, wind direction, wind barbs) are available here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15090857\"><em>https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15090857&nbsp;</em></a></p>\n<p>Continuous data availability consists of</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Extensive Operation Period (EOP) with 3 DWLs from June 10, 2022 &ndash; March 05, 2024</li>\n<li>Two Intensive Observation Periods (IOPs) with six DWL over 9 weeks in September 2023 to December 2023.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Detailed data availability per site along with weather conditions and classifications can be found in the files \"paris_dwl_L3VX.XX_data_availability_weather.pdf\" and \"paris_dwl_L3VX.XX_data_availability_weather.xlsx\".</p>\n<p>Data are provided in daily NetCDF files in two temporal resolutions of 10 minutes (\"_600s\") and 1 hour (\"_3600s\"). All dates / times are in UTC. Files are packaged by year and month using the following name convention \"paris_dwl_L3VX.XX_YYYY_MM_RRRRs.tar.gz\", where X.XX is the version number, YYYY refers to the year, (2022-2024) MM to the month of the year (01-12), and RRRR is the time resolution with \"600s\" and \"3600s\".</p>\n<p>NetCDF files contain the following fields:</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><em>standard_name</em>&nbsp;(Variable name)</td>\n<td>Dimensions</td>\n<td>Description</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>time</em></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Timestamp: end of time interval. 600 s and 3600 s time intervals are provided, in separate data files (600 s e.g. 00:00:01 &rarr; 00:10:00 and 3600 s e.g. 00:00:01 &rarr; 01:00:00). All variables are harmonised to this resolution as averages (e.g. wind) or percentage occurrence (e.g. flags)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>altitude</em></td>\n<td>1&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Altitude of centre of each measurement gate above mean sea level (m). Harmonised gates are 25 m from 0 &ndash; 6500 m with values linearly interpolated to this resolution&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>station</em></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Measurement location identifier (see table below), all are listed even if no valid data are retrieved during the file&rsquo;s date.&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>eastward_wind</em> (u)&nbsp;</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Mean eastward wind component (m s-1) using all valid samples within time interval&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>northward_wind (v)&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Mean northward wind component (m s-1) using all valid samples within time interval&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>wind_speed (ws)&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Horizontal wind speed calculated from <em>eastward_wind</em> and <em>northward_wind</em> (m s-1)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>wind_from_direction (wd)&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Horizontal wind direction calculated from <em>eastward_wind</em> and <em>northward_wind</em> (degrees from true north)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>system_id&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Serial number of sensor deployed at station at a given time&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>latitude (station_lat)&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Latitude of the measurement station (degrees, decimal, WGS84)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>longitude (station_lon)&nbsp;</em></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Longitude of the measurement station (degrees, decimal, WGS84)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>station_altitude&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>1&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Measurement station height above ground level (m).&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div>\n<p>Ground level is the &ldquo;street&rdquo; level so if the station is on a rooftop, the height will accounts for the building height and any mounting structure&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>station_height&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>1&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Average height of station above sea level (reference_geoid: EGM96) (m)&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>n_rays_in_scan&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>2&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Number of rays in a scan. e.g. 12 for a VAD scan that has 12 samples within one scan&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>n_pulses&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>2&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Number of pulses in a given ray. More pulses, the higher the integration time&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>raw_gate_length&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>2&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Gate length prior to L3 aggregation (m)&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>flag_suspect_retrieval_warn&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>3&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Percentage of values within time interval with retrieval warning not linked to low signal (flag_low_signal_warn_pc) or out of range (flag_ws_out_of_range_removed_pc). Retrievals retained but treat with caution&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>flag_suspect_retrieval_removed&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>3&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Percentage of values within time interval with retrieval error not linked to low signal (flag_low_signal_warn_pc) or out of range (flag_ws_out_of_range_removed_pc). Data removed&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>flag_low_signal_warn&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>3&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Percentage of values within time interval with a low SNR. Retrievals retained but treat with caution&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>flag_low_signal_removed&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>3&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Percentage of values within time interval with a low SNR. Retrieval rejected&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><em>flag_ws_out_of_range_removed&nbsp;</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>3&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>Percentage of values within time interval with wind speed outside reasonable retrievable range (&gt; 60 m s-1) (i.e. removed). Evaluated after all other retrieval QC&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Version history</strong></p>\n<p>Version 1.42</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Selected additional values at the station PAROIS have been flagged and/or removed due to suspicion of an instrument malfunction. Data have been compared to a co-located SODAR to assess data quality (see manuscript for details)</li>\n<li>Weather data files (paris_dwl_L3V1.42_data_availability_weather.xlsx and paris_dwl_L3V1.42_data_availability_weather.pdf) have been corrected for an error in the column \"Precipitation (mm day-1) MF Montsouris Weather Station\" (previously incorrect atribution to day), for the correct highlighting of weekend days and they have been expanded to include sunrise, sunset and solar noon times.</li>\n<li>Added the processing code adapted from the halo-reader package (halo-reader-morrison-fork.zip)</li>\n<li>Added the dataset production code (paris-harmonised-dwl-morrison-fork.zip)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
